in 1865 before germany was germany it  was numerous smaller states many of  which were ruled by kings and had been  so for many centuries yet in 1871  germany was unified and all of these  kingdoms had been incorporated into the  german empire under the leadership of  the german emperor and generally in  european empires there was only room for  one royal family the imperial one which  raises the question what became of these  other german kings and their kingdoms so  in 1865 there were six kingdoms in the  german world hanover prussia saxony  voitenberg bavaria and bohemia they were  all part of the german confederation the  successor to the holy roman empire which  like that was also led by the ruler of  austria who had been butting heads with  the leaders of prussia over who was to  lead the german-speaking world these  tensions soon led to war with all of the  kingdom siding with austria over prussia  which may not have been the best choice  since prussia with the help of italy  would go on to win this saw prussia grow  to this annexing the kingdom of hanover  and thereby reducing the number of kings  to five prussian leadership had wanted  to annex saxony but given its king's  close relationship with the austrian  emperor its continued independence was a  condition for peace now the prussians  could have kept fighting but its  chancellor otto von bismarck wanted the  war over quickly because he was  concerned that france would join the war  on the side of austria which would make  things much more difficult for them as  such peace and prussia form the north  german confederation which saxony joined  the next year having previously agreed  to do so so what happened to saxony's  king well nothing the north german  confederation was a federal nation whose  states were fairly autonomous this was  because for bismarck ousting the king of  saxony would make the other kingdoms  much more nervous about joining a german  state as such the king of saxony could  stay but in return foreign policy would  be run from berlin and this framework  was in place when in 1871 these states  were added to the german empire these  three kings had mixed feelings about the  empire's creation which is why when it  was formed in the wake of france's  defeat wilhelm wasn't made the emperor  of germany but the german emperor since  the first title meant that he  technically ruled over their lands and  he was their superior whereas the second  title meant that he was the first  amongst equals obviously they weren't  his equal since brussels control over  the german empire was basically absolute  but they got to keep doing fun king  stuff so what exactly happened to them  well the smaller german kings met the  same end as the german emperor in 1918  at the end of world war one after the  kaiser's abdication and flight germany  was declared to be a republic which saw  two kings frederick augustus iii of  saxony and ludwig iii of bavaria  abdicate a few days after the emperor  frederick augustus had hoped to maintain  his position but he was unpopular and  blamed for the troubles of the war and  so off he went the last king to abdicate  was william ii of voitenberg who had  been fairly popular with his people but  the revolution across germany as a whole  meant that his position was untenable  royal titles were abolished there in  1919 and whilst they were no longer  kings they got to keep their stuff and  heard a great deal of social prestige  throughout the years of the weimar  republic but despite their high social  standing after this no king nor royal  would ever return to germany i hope you  enjoyed this episode and thank you for  watching with a special thanks to my  patrons james bisonette kelly moneymaker  corso wolfe jerry lamden jordan longley  adam stalter y and hockey captain cydog  rod d martin marvin castle spencer  lightfoot gustav swan common yoon  boogery wiggly matthew shipley marcus  asner the mc whopper aaron the white max  and flauri